From 1c2e0f41ba10a7b1472f82ebd1072474b611b149 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 08:44:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Desktop sidebar: one icon size, one row height, a 72px rail

The rail mixed 22, 24 and 32px icons in 44px and auto-height tiles, so
neighbours read at different sizes. Every icon in the rail is now 20px
(the mark 28px, New session a 40px circle), every destination is a 56px
tile with an 11px label, and the bottom actions are 40px buttons. The rail
is 72px instead of 88px (--app-sidebar follows). The expanded desktop
sidebar uses the same 20px icons. The phone drawer keeps its Figma 24px
icons. Staging only (RELEASES.sidebarRail).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Je1v64McNyB6XEu6gFgM4C
